    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starting 1 July) with a single new home for the fiscal-year arithmetic, and reused it everywhere it was needed.\n\n**New utility \u2014 `util/FiscalYears.java`** (single responsibility: fiscal-year math):\n- `startYear(date)` \u2014 the calendar year in which a date's fiscal year begins (its own year from 1 July onward, else the previous year).\n- `label(date)` \u2014 the `FY<YY>` string (null-safe).\n- `elapsedBetween(from, to)` \u2014 number of 1 July boundaries crossed.\n\n**Wired it into the three date-derived values:**\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 new `fiscalYear(owner)` derivation mapped to a new `fiscalYear` DTO field, sourced from the business-day-adjusted `registrationDate`.\n- `util/MembershipNumbers.java` \u2014 the `-M<YY>` year segment now uses `FiscalYears.startYear(...)` instead of the raw calendar year.\n- `util/MembershipLevels.java` \u2014 tenure now counts elapsed fiscal years (`FiscalYears.elapsedBetween >= TENURE_FISCAL_YEARS`), replacing the old `TENURE_DAYS = 365` / `ChronoUnit.DAYS` window. `TENURE_DAYS` became `TENURE_FISCAL_YEARS = 1`.\n\n**Contract/docs:**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the `fiscalYear` schema property, and updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to reflect the fiscal-year basis.\n\nEach class keeps its role: the mapper exposes values, `MembershipNumbers`/`MembershipLevels` own their respective derivations, and all fiscal-year logic lives once in `FiscalYears`. The new `coreReturnsFiscalYear` acceptance test and the full suite pass; the audit log confirms behaviour (e.g. `registrationDate=2026-09-21 \u2192 membershipNumber=\u2026-M26`, fiscal year `FY26`).\n\nOne design decision worth flagging: I identify a fiscal year by its **starting** calendar year (1 July 2026\u201330 June 2027 \u2192 `FY26`) and award tenure points once **at least one** fiscal-year boundary has been crossed. Both are documented in the code/OpenAPI. If your organisation labels fiscal years by the *ending* year, or wants a stricter \"more than one full fiscal year\" tenure threshold, those are one-line changes in `FiscalYears`/`MembershipLevels` \u2014 let me know.",
